  "result": "I fixed the bug. `IntRange` with `clamp=True` and an open bound (`min_open` or `max_open`) returned a value outside the allowed range. The `test_types.py` tests pass (43 passed, 2 skipped). I did not run the full suite.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py` moved away from an open bound instead of into the range. It computed `bound - dir`, where `dir` is 1 when clamping to a minimum and -1 when clamping to a maximum. For example, `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turned `-5` into `-1`, which is still invalid. I changed it to `bound + dir`, so that case now gives `1`.\n\nI added two regression cases to `test_range` in `tests/test_types.py`: a min-open case (`-5` becomes `1`) and a max-open case (`9` becomes `4`).\n\nOne slip along the way: I made an edit call with a wrong file path by mistake. It failed because the file didn't exist, so nothing changed.",
